ing between different themes','','none'),(4927,_binary 'Configuring block settings','','none'),(4928,_binary 'You can control the visibility of a block by restricting it to specific pages, content types, and/or roles by setting the appropriate options under <em>Visibility settings</em> of the block configuration.','','none'),(4929,_binary 'Unless you\'re experiencing problems with pagers related to this field, you should leave this at 0. If using multiple pagers on one page you may need to set this number to a higher value so as not to conflict within the ?page= array. Large values will add a lot of commas to your URLs, so avoid if possible.','','none'),(4930,_binary 'Pager ID: @id','','none'),(4931,_binary 'Enter the name of the configuration file without the <em>.yml</em> extension. (e.g. <em>system.site</em>)','','none'),(4932,_binary 'The sender\'s email','','10.5.6'),(4933,_binary 'The email of the person that is sending the contact message.','','none'),(4934,_binary 'Relate file entities to their usage.','','none'),(4935,_binary 'Managing and displaying file fields','','none'),(4936,_binary 'Allowing file extensions','','none'),(4937,_binary 'In the field settings, you can define the allowed file extensions (for example <em>pdf docx psd</em>) for the files that will be uploaded with the file field.','','none'),(4938,_binary 'Restricting the maximum file size','','none'),(4939,_binary 'The maximum file size that users can upload is limited by PHP settings of the server, but you can restrict by entering the desired value as the <em>Maximum upload size</em> setting. The maximum file size is automatically displayed to users in the help text of the file field.','','none'),(4940,_binary 'Displaying files and descriptions','','none'),(4941,_binary 'In the field settings, you can allow users to toggle whether individual files are displayed. In the display settings, you can then choose one of the following formats: <ul><li><em>Generic file</em> displays links to the files and adds icons that symbolize the file extensions. If <em>descriptions</em> are enabled and have been submitted, then the description is displayed instead of the file name.</li><li><em>URL to file</em> displays the full path to the file as plain text.</li><li><em>Table of files</em> lists links to the files and the file sizes in a table.</li><li><em>RSS enclosure</em> only displays the first file, and only in a RSS feed, formatted according to the RSS 2.0 syntax for enclosures.</li></ul> A file can still be linked to directly by its URI even if it is not displayed.','','none'),(4942,_binary 'Flag to control whether this file should be displayed when viewing content','','none'),(4943,_binary 'The log entry explaining the changes in this revision.','','10.5.6'),(4944,_binary 'At least one authentication provider must be defined for resource @id','','none'),(4945,_binary 'At least one format must be defined for resource @id','','none'),(4946,_binary 'The ID of the shortcut.','','none'),(4947,_binary 'The UUID of the shortcut.','','none'),(4948,_binary 'The bundle of the shortcut.','','none'),(4949,_binary 'Weight among shortcuts in the same shortcut set.','','none'),(4950,_binary 'Route name','','none'),(4951,_binary 'The language code of the shortcut.','','none'),(4952,_binary 'Shortcut link','','10.5.6'),(4953,_binary 'Rebuild access','','none'),(4954,_binary 'The rebuild_access setting is enabled in settings.php. It is recommended to have this setting disabled unless you are performing a rebuild.','','none'),(4955,_binary 'Relate nodes to taxonomy terms, specifying which vocabulary or vocabularies to use. This relationship will cause duplicated records if there are multiple terms.','','10.5.6'),(4956,_binary 'Taxonomy term ID','','none'),(4957,_binary 'Taxonomy term name','','10.5.6'),(4958,_binary 'Return to site content','','10.5.6'),(4959,_binary 'Preferred admin language code','','10.5.6'),(4960,_binary 'The user\'s preferred language code for receiving emails and viewing the site.','','none'),(4961,_binary 'Preferred language code','','10.5.6'),(4962,_binary 'The user\'s preferred language code for viewing administration pages.','','none'),(4963,_binary 'The name of this user.','','none'),(4964,_binary 'The password of this user (hashed).','','none'),(4965,_binary 'The email of this user.','','none'),(4966,_binary 'The timezone of this user.','','none'),(4967,_binary 'The time that the user was created.','','none'),(4968,_binary 'Initial email','','10.5.6'),(4969,_binary 'User ID from route context','','10.5.6'),(4970,_binary 'The Views module provides a back end to fetch information from content, user accounts, taxonomy terms, and other entities from the database and present it to the user as a grid, HTML list, table, unformatted list, etc. The resulting displays are known generally as <em>views</em>.','','none'),(4971,_binary 'Adding functionality to administrative pages','','none'),(4972,_binary 'The Views module adds functionality to some core administration pages. For example, <em>admin/content</em> uses Views to filter and sort content. With Views uninstalled, <em>admin/content</em> is more limited.','','none'),(4973,_binary 'Expanding Views functionality','','none'),(4974,_binary 'Changing the title here means it cannot be dynamically altered anymore.','','none'),(4975,_binary 'Validate @label','','none'),(4976,_binary 'Validate user has access to the %name','','10.5.6'),(4977,_binary 'Multiple arguments','','10.5.6'),(4978,_binary 'Single ID','','10.5.6'),(4979,_binary 'One or more IDs separated by , or +','','10.5.6'),(4980,_binary 'Tag based','','10.5.6'),(4981,_binary 'Tag based caching of data. Caches will persist until any related cache tags are invalidated.','','none'),(4982,_binary 'Name and description','','10.5.6'),(4983,_binary 'Administrative tags','','10.5.6'),(4984,_binary 'Enter a comma-separated list of words to describe your view.','','10.5.6'),(4985,_binary 'Click <em>Save</em>.','','10.5.6'),