one'),(5011,_binary 'Creating short text fields','','none'),(5012,_binary 'Creating long text fields','','none'),(5013,_binary 'Trimming the text length','','none'),(5014,_binary 'On the <em>Manage display</em> page you can choose to display a trimmed version of the text, and if so, where to cut off the text.','','none'),(5015,_binary 'Displaying summaries instead of trimmed text','','none'),(5016,_binary 'Using text formats and editors','','none'),(5017,_binary 'Left','Text alignment','none'),(5018,_binary 'Center','Text alignment','none'),(5019,_binary 'Right','Text alignment','none'),(5020,_binary 'State label','','none'),(5021,_binary '%name: may not be longer than @max characters.','','none'),(5022,_binary 'A breakpoint separates the height or width of viewports (screens, printers, and other media output types) into steps. For instance, a width breakpoint of 40em creates two steps: one for widths up to 40em and one for widths above 40em. Breakpoints can be used to define when layouts should shift from one form to another, when images should be resized, and other changes that need to respond to changes in viewport height or width.','','none'),(5023,_binary 'Resolution multiplier','','none'),(5024,_binary 'Resolution multipliers are a measure of the viewport\'s device resolution, defined to be the ratio between the physical pixel size of the active device and the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Device_independent_pixel\">device-independent pixel</a> size. The Breakpoint module defines multipliers of 1, 1.5, and 2; when defining breakpoints, modules and themes can define which multipliers apply to each breakpoint.','','10.5.6'),(5025,_binary 'Modules and themes can use the API provided by the Breakpoint module to define breakpoints and breakpoint groups, and to assign resolution multipliers to breakpoints.','','none'),(5026,_binary 'Comment author name','Validation','none'),(5027,_binary 'Changing the text format to %text_format will permanently remove content that is not allowed in that text format.<br><br>Save your changes before switching the text format to avoid losing data.','','10.5.6'),(5028,_binary 'Entity view display','','10.5.6'),(5029,_binary 'Managing and displaying entity reference fields','','none'),(5030,_binary 'Selecting reference type','','none'),(5031,_binary 'In the field settings you can select which entity type you want to create a reference to.','','none'),(5032,_binary 'Filtering and sorting reference fields','','none'),(5033,_binary 'Depending on the chosen entity type, additional filtering and sorting options are available for the list of entities that can be referred to, in the field settings. For example, the list of users can be filtered by role and sorted by name or ID.','','none'),(5034,_binary 'Displaying a reference','','none'),(5035,_binary 'An entity reference can be displayed as a simple label with or without a link to the entity. Alternatively, the referenced entity can be displayed as a teaser (or any other available view mode) inside the referencing entity.','','none'),(5036,_binary 'Managing text formats','','none'),(5037,_binary 'Assigning roles to text formats','','none'),(5038,_binary 'Selecting filters','','none'),(5039,_binary 'Each filter can have additional configuration options. For example, for the \"Limit allowed HTML tags\" filter you need to define the list of HTML tags that the filter leaves in the text.','','none'),(5040,_binary 'When creating or editing data in a field that has text formats enabled, users can select the format under the field from the Text format select list.','','none'),(5041,_binary 'Import behavior','','none'),(5042,_binary 'The keywords to search for.','','10.5.6'),(5043,_binary 'Managing and displaying list fields','','none'),(5044,_binary 'Defining option keys and labels','','none'),(5045,_binary 'When you define the list options you can define a key and a label for each option in the list. The label will be shown to the users while the key gets stored in the database.','','none'),(5046,_binary 'Choosing list field type','','none'),(5047,_binary 'There are three types of list fields, which store different types of data: <em>float</em>, <em>integer</em> or, <em>text</em>. The <em>float</em> type allows storing approximate decimal values. The <em>integer</em> type allows storing whole numbers, such as years (for example, 2012) or values (for example, 1, 2, 5, 305). The <em>text</em> list field type allows storing text values. No matter which type of list field you choose, you can define whatever labels you wish for data entry.','','none'),(5048,_binary 'Dependency of required module @module','','none'),(5049,_binary 'Some of the pending updates cannot be applied because their dependencies were not met.','','none'),(5050,_binary 'The vocabulary to which the term is assigned.','','none'),(5051,_binary 'Viewing tours','','none'),(5052,_binary 'If a tour is available on a page, a <em>Tour</em> button will be visible in the toolbar. If you click this button the first tip of the tour will appear. The tour continues after clicking the <em>Next</em> button in the tip. To see a tour users must have the permission <em>Access tour</em> and JavaScript must be enabled in the browser','','none'),(5053,_binary 'Creating tours','','none'),(5054,_binary 'Managing user account fields','','none'),(5055,_binary 'The date the taxonomy was most recently updated.','','none'),(5056,_binary 'An entity field containing a UNIX timestamp of when the entity has been last updated.','','none'),(5057,_binary 'An entity field containing a UNIX timestamp of when the entity has been created.','','none'),(5058,_binary 'An entity field for storing a serialized array of values.','','none'),(5059,_binary 'Timestamp value','','10.5.6'),(5060,_binary 'Sends the message as plain text, using PHP\'s native mail() function.','','none'),(5061,_binary 'Mail collector','','none'),(5062,_binary 'Does not send the message, but stores it in Drupal withi