nary 'Text (formatted, long) settings','','none'),(5914,_binary 'Text (formatted, long, with summary) settings','','none'),(5915,_binary 'Formatted text default display format settings','','none'),(5916,_binary 'Summary or trimmed formatted text display format settings','','none'),(5917,_binary 'Text (formatted)','','10.5.6'),(5918,_binary 'Text (formatted, long)','','10.5.6'),(5919,_binary 'Text (formatted, long, with summary)','','10.5.6'),(5920,_binary 'Require email verification when a visitor creates an account','','none'),(5921,_binary '- No preference -','','none'),(5922,_binary 'Notify user when account is canceled','','none'),(5923,_binary 'The time that the user was last edited.','','none'),(5924,_binary 'Display the referenced author user entity.','','none'),(5925,_binary 'Add a read-more link if output is trimmed','','10.5.6'),(5926,_binary '@entity_type revision','','10.5.6'),(5927,_binary '@entity_type revisions','','10.5.6'),(5928,_binary 'Include reset button (resets all applied exposed filters)','','none'),(5929,_binary 'The <em>Exposed items per page</em> field\'s options must include the value from the <em>Items per page</em> field (@items_per_page).','','none'),(5930,_binary 'REST export settings','','none'),(5931,_binary 'Provide a REST export','','none'),(5932,_binary 'REST export path','','none'),(5933,_binary 'Default value callback','','none'),(5934,_binary 'URI as link display format settings','','none'),(5935,_binary 'Timestamp ago display format settings','','none'),(5936,_binary 'Link to URI','','none'),(5937,_binary 'Field storage','','10.5.6'),(5938,_binary '%field settings for %bundle','','10.5.6'),(5939,_binary 'The minimum allowed image size expressed as WIDTH×HEIGHT (e.g. 640×480). Leave blank for no restriction. If a smaller image is uploaded, it will be rejected.','','none'),(5940,_binary 'Disabling drag-and-drop functionality','','10.5.6'),(5941,_binary 'Improving table accessibility','','none'),(5942,_binary 'Views tables include semantic markup to improve accessibility. Data cells are automatically associated with header cells through id and header attributes. To improve the accessibility of your tables you can add descriptive elements within the Views table settings. The <em>caption</em> element can introduce context for a table, making it easier to understand. The <em>summary</em> element can provide an overview of how the data has been organized and how to navigate the table. Both the caption and summary are visible by default and also implemented according to HTML5 guidelines.','','none'),(5943,_binary 'OPML field options','','none'),(5944,_binary 'Testing multilingual','','none'),(5945,_binary 'Minimal profile for running tests with a multilingual installer.','','none'),(5946,_binary 'Muted','','none'),(5947,_binary 'Broken/Missing','','10.5.6'),(5948,_binary 'Entity Reference reference access','Validation','none'),(5949,_binary 'You do not have access to the referenced entity (%type: %id).','','none'),(5950,_binary '@label ID','','10.5.6'),(5951,_binary 'Email','Validation','none'),(5952,_binary 'Comments are responses to content.','','none'),(5953,_binary 'Filename: %name','','none'),(5954,_binary 'Recipient username','','none'),(5955,_binary 'You can align images (<code>data-align=\"center\"</code>), but also videos, blockquotes, and so on.','','10.5.6'),(5956,_binary 'You can caption images (<code>data-caption=\"Text\"</code>), but also videos, blockquotes, and so on.','','10.5.6'),(5957,_binary 'Making this field required is recommended.','','none'),(5958,_binary 'The title attribute is used as a tooltip when the mouse hovers over the image. Enabling this field is not recommended as it can cause problems with screen readers.','','none'),(5959,_binary 'Image convert failed using the %toolkit toolkit on %path (%mimetype)','','none'),(5960,_binary 'The domain may not be left blank for %language.','','none'),(5961,_binary 'Leave preview?','','none'),(5962,_binary 'Leave preview','','none'),(5963,_binary 'Search for @keywords','','none'),(5964,_binary 'Instructs the toolkit to save the image with a specified extension.','','none'),(5965,_binary 'Set a new image','','none'),(5966,_binary 'The text with the text format applied.','','none'),(5967,_binary 'Processed summary','','none'),(5968,_binary 'The summary text with the text format applied.','','none'),(5969,_binary 'Tabs are buttons, displayed in a bar across the top of the screen. Some tabs execute an action (such as starting Edit mode), while other tabs toggle which tray is open.','','none'),(5970,_binary 'Trays','','none'),(5971,_binary 'Trays are usually lists of links, which can be hierarchical like a menu. If a tray has been toggled open, it is displayed either vertically or horizontally below the tab bar, depending on the browser width. Only one tray may be open at a time. If you click another tab, that tray will replace the tray being displayed. In wide browser widths, the user has the ability to toggle from vertical to horizontal, using a link at the bottom or right of the tray. Hierarchical menus only have open/close behavior in vertical mode; if you display a tray containing a hierarchical menu horizontally, only the top-level links will be available.','','none'),(5972,_binary 'Your account will be blocked and you will no longer be able to log in. All of your content will remain attributed to your username.','','none'),(5973,_binary 'Language of the translation of user information','','none'),(5974,_binary 'Preferred language of the user','','none'),(5975,_binary 'Preferred admin language','','none'),(5976,_binary 'Preferred administrative language of the user','','none'),(5977,_binary 'Cache metadata','','none'),(5978,_binary 'Cache contexts','','none'),(5979,_binary 'Path is empty.','','none'),(5980,_binary 'No query allowed.','','none'),(5981,_binary 'Invalid path. Valid characters are alphanumerics as well as \"-\", \".\", \"_\" and \"~\".','','none'),(5982,_binary 'Wrapping'