mine stacking of the chart. Generally this will be the same field as what you select for the \"Label field\" below. If you do not have more than one \"Provides data\" field below, there will be nothing to stack. If you want to have another series displayed, use a \"Chart attachment\" display, and set it to attach to this display.','','10.5.6'),(11360,_binary 'Site Default','','10.5.6'),(11361,_binary 'Highcharts','','10.5.6'),(11362,_binary 'Charting library','','10.5.6'),(11363,_binary '<p>The site default charting library has not been set yet, or it does not support chart type options. Please ensure that you have correctly <a href=\"/admin/config/content/charts\">configured the chart module</a>.</p>','','10.5.6'),(11364,_binary 'Please select a valid charting library.','','10.5.6'),(11365,_binary '@label_singular','','10.5.6'),(11366,_binary 'The settings on this page are used to set\n        <strong>default</strong> settings. They do not affect existing charts.\n        To make a new chart, create a new view and select the display format of\n        \"Chart.\" Or use a Charts Block and add your own data inside that block.\n        You can also attach a Chart field to your content (or other entity)\n        type and add your data within the Chart field.','','10.5.6'),(11367,_binary 'Area Range','','10.5.6'),(11368,_binary 'Bar','','10.5.6'),(11369,_binary 'Boxplot','','10.5.6'),(11370,_binary 'Bubble','','10.5.6'),(11371,_binary 'Donut','','10.5.6'),(11372,_binary 'Gauge','','10.5.6'),(11373,_binary 'Heatmap','','10.5.6'),(11374,_binary 'Line','','10.5.6'),(11375,_binary 'Pie','','10.5.6'),(11376,_binary 'Scatter','','10.5.6'),(11377,_binary 'Spline','','10.5.6'),(11378,_binary 'Solid Gauge','','10.5.6'),(11379,_binary 'Dumbbell','','10.5.6'),(11380,_binary 'Chart type','','10.5.6'),(11381,_binary 'Chart title','','10.5.6'),(11382,_binary 'Chart subtitle','','10.5.6'),(11383,_binary 'Not all charting libraries support this option. Disabled until there is a title value.','','10.5.6'),(11384,_binary 'Add a new default color','','10.5.6'),(11385,_binary 'Outside','','10.5.6'),(11386,_binary 'Inside','','10.5.6'),(11387,_binary 'Title position','','10.5.6'),(11388,_binary 'Not all of these will apply to your selected library.','','10.5.6'),(11389,_binary 'Enable tooltips','','10.5.6'),(11390,_binary 'Show data details on mouse over? Note: unavailable for print or on mobile devices.','','10.5.6'),(11391,_binary 'Enable data labels','','10.5.6'),(11392,_binary 'Show data details as labels on chart? Note: recommended for print or on mobile devices.','','10.5.6'),(11393,_binary 'Enable data markers','','10.5.6'),(11394,_binary 'Show data markers (points) on line charts?','','10.5.6'),(11395,_binary 'Connect nulls','','10.5.6'),(11396,_binary 'Connect interrupted points on line charts?','','10.5.6'),(11397,_binary 'Legend position','','10.5.6'),(11398,_binary 'transparent','','10.5.6'),(11399,_binary 'Leave blank for a transparent background.','','10.5.6'),(11400,_binary 'Make chart three-dimensional (3D)','','10.5.6'),(11401,_binary 'Transform cartesian charts into the polar coordinate system','','10.5.6'),(11402,_binary 'auto','','10.5.6'),(11403,_binary 'If dimensions are left empty, the chart will fill its containing element.','','10.5.6'),(11404,_binary 'Gauge maximum value','','10.5.6'),(11405,_binary 'Gauge minimum value','','10.5.6'),(11406,_binary 'Green minimum value','','10.5.6'),(11407,_binary 'Green maximum value','','10.5.6'),(11408,_binary 'Yellow minimum value','','10.5.6'),(11409,_binary 'Yellow maximum value','','10.5.6'),(11410,_binary 'Red minimum value','','10.5.6'),(11411,_binary 'Red maximum value','','10.5.6'),(11412,_binary 'Gauge settings','','10.5.6'),(11413,_binary 'Expose color changer','','10.5.6'),(11414,_binary 'Display a widget that enables users to switch the chart colors.','','10.5.6'),(11415,_binary 'Custom title','','10.5.6'),(11416,_binary '0°','','10.5.6'),(11417,_binary '15°','','10.5.6'),(11418,_binary '30°','','10.5.6'),(11419,_binary '45°','','10.5.6'),(11420,_binary '60°','','10.5.6'),(11421,_binary '90°','','10.5.6'),(11422,_binary 'Labels rotation','','10.5.6'),(11423,_binary 'Horizontal axis','','10.5.6'),(11424,_binary 'Value range','','10.5.6'),(11425,_binary 'Value range minimum','','10.5.6'),(11426,_binary 'Value prefix','','10.5.6'),(11427,_binary 'Value suffix','','10.5.6'),(11428,_binary 'Decimal count','','10.5.6'),(11429,_binary 'Enforce a certain number of decimal-place digits in displayed values.','','10.5.6'),(11430,_binary 'Vertical axis','','10.5.6'),(11431,_binary '<p>Charts is designed to be generic enough to work with multiple charting libraries. If you would like settings that apply to all Highcharts charts, you can <a href=\"https://www.drupal.org/project/issues/charts\" target=\"_blank\">submit a ticket</a> to have a setting added here, in the Highcharts-specific settings.</p>','','10.5.6'),(11432,_binary 'Enable Highcharts\' \"3D\" library','','10.5.6'),(11433,_binary 'Highcharts 3D module is a separate library that enables 3D charts. See <a href=\"https://www.highcharts.com/docs/chart-concepts/3d-charts\" target=\"_blank\">Highcharts 3D documentation</a> for more information.','','10.5.6'),(11434,_binary 'Enable Highcharts\' \"Accessibility\" library','','10.5.6'),(11435,_binary 'Highcharts Accessibility module is a separate library that enables accessibility features. See <a href=\"https://www.highcharts.com/docs/chart-concepts/accessibility\" target=\"_blank\">Highcharts Accessibility documentation</a> for more information.','','10.5.6'),(11436,_binary 'Enable Highcharts\' \"Annotations\" library','','10.5.6'),(11437,_binary 'Highcharts Annotations module is a separate library that enables annotations. See <a href=\"https://www.highcharts.com/docs/advanced-chart-features/annotations-module\" target=\"_blank\">Highcharts Annotations documentation</a> for more information.','','10.5.6'),(11438,_binary 'Enable Highcharts\' \"Boost\" library','','10.5.6'),(11439,_binary 'Highcharts Boost module is a separate library that enables faster rendering of charts. See <a href=\"https://www.highcharts.com/docs/advanced-chart-features/boost-module\" target=\"_blank\">Highcharts Boost documentation</a> for more information.','','10.5.6'),(11440,_binary 'Enable Highcharts\' \"Color Axis\" library','','10.5.6'),(11441,_binary 'Highcharts Color Axis module is a separate library that enables color axis. See <a href=\"https://www.highcharts.com/docs/chart-and-series-types/color-axis\" target=\"_blank\">Highcharts Color Axis documentation</a> for more information.','','10.5.6'),(11442,_binary 'Enable Highcharts\' \"Data\" library','','10.5.6'),(11443,_binary 'Highcharts Data module is a separate library that enables data import and export. See <a href=\"https://www.highcharts.com/docs/working-with-data/data-module\" target=\"_blank\">Highcharts Data documentation</a> for more information.','','10.5.6'),(11444,_binary 'Enable Highcharts\' \"Dumbbell\" library','','10.5.6'),(11445,_binary 'Highcharts Dumbbell module is a separate library that enables the dumbbell chart style. See <a href=\"https://www.highcharts.com/docs/chart-and-series-types/dumbbell-series\" target=\"_blank\">Highcharts Dumbbell documentation</a> for more information.','','10.5.6'),(11446,_binary 'Enable Highcharts\' \"Exporting\" library','','10.5.6'),(11447,_binary 'Highcharts Exporting module is a separate library that enables exporting charts. See <a href=\"https://www.highcharts.com/docs/export-module/export-module-overview\" target=\"_blank\">Highcharts Exporting documentation</a> for more information.','','10.5.6'),(11448,_binary 'Enable Highcharts\' \"Heatmap\" library','','10.5.6'),(11449,_binary 'Highcharts Heatmap module is a separate library that enables heatmap charts. See <a href=\"https://www.highcharts.com/docs/chart-and-series-types/heatmap-series\" target=\"_blank\">Highcharts Heatmap documentation</a> for more information.','','10.5.6'),(11450,_binary 'Enable Highcharts\' \"No Data\" library','','10.5.6'),(11451,_binary 'Highcharts No Data module is a separate library that enables no data message. See <a href=\"https://api.highcharts.com/highcharts/noData\" target=\"_blank\">Highcharts No Data documentation</a> for more information.','','10.5.6'),(11452,_binary 'Enable Highcharts\' \"Texture\" library','','10.5.6'),(11453,_binary 'Highcharts Texture module is a separate library that enables texture fill. See <a href=\"https://www.highcharts.com/docs/chart-design-and-style/pattern-fills\" target=\"_blank\">Highcharts Texture documentation</a> for more information.','','10.5.6'),(11454,_binary 'Enable Highcharts\' \"Solid Gauge\" library','','10.5.6'),(11455,_binary 'Highcharts Texture module is a separate library that enables texture fill. See <a href=\"https://api.highcharts.com/highcharts/series.solidgauge\" target=\"_blank\">Solid Gauge documentation</a> for more information.','','10.5.6'),(11456,_binary 'Auto','','10.5.6'),(11457,_binary 'Legend layout','','10.5.6'),(11458,_binary 'Legend background color','','10.5.6'),(11459,_binary 'Legend border width','','10.5.6'),(11460,_binary 'Enable legend shadow','','10.5.6'),(11461,_binary 'Item style color','','10.5.6'),(11462,_binary 'Leave blank for a dark gray font.','','10.5.6'),(11463,_binary 'Ellipsis','','10.5.6'),(11464,_binary 'Text overflow','','10.5.6'),(11465,_binary 'Item Style','','10.5.6'),(11466,_binary 'Legend Settings','','10.5.6'),(11467,_binary 'Download @format','','10.5.6'),(11468,_binary 'The text for the @format download menu item.','','10.5.6'),(11469,_binary 'Exit fullscreen','','10.5.6'),(11470,_binary 'Exporting module only. The text for the menu item to exit the chart from full screen.','','10.5.6'),(11471,_binary 'Hide data','','10.5.6'),(11472,_binary 'The text for the menu item.','','10.5.6'),(11473,_binary 'The loading text that appears when the chart is set into the loading state following a call to 