d apply styles from the CSS files instead of inline styles. For example for dark mode support. See <a href=\":url\" target=\"_blank\">chart.styledMode</a> for more information.','','10.5.6'),(11503,_binary '@library settings','','10.5.6'),(11504,_binary 'Chart configuration','','10.5.6'),(11505,_binary 'Charts Settings','','10.5.6'),(11506,_binary 'Reset to default configurations','','10.5.6'),(11507,_binary 'This text will be displayed on the @mode_label list page.','','10.5.6'),(11508,_binary 'Enable this @display-mode for the following @bundle-label types:','','10.5.6'),(11509,_binary 'This @display-mode will still be available for the rest of the @bundle-label types if not checked here, but it will not be enabled by default.','','10.5.6'),(11510,_binary 'Exposed Chart Type','','10.5.6'),(11511,_binary 'Scatter Field','','10.5.6'),(11512,_binary 'Bubble Field','','10.5.6'),(11513,_binary 'Numeric Array','','10.5.6'),(11514,_binary 'Use this field for your data field in a bubble chart.','','10.5.6'),(11515,_binary 'Use this field for exposing chart type.','','10.5.6'),(11516,_binary 'Use this field for your data field in a chart of 1-10 array items.','','10.5.6'),(11517,_binary 'Use this field for your data field in a scatter plot.','','10.5.6'),(11518,_binary 'An entity field containing data for a chart item','','10.5.6');
